# Replies to players' BUG, TYPO and IDEA reports (src/bugreply.c).
# Each entry: '@ <id> <yyyy-mm-dd> <Player>', then the reply; a blank line
# is a paragraph break, and the next '@' ends it. At every boot an entry
# dated within 30 days whose id is on no note yet is posted as a note from
# the Immortals to that player, subject "Re: your report [<id>]". Ids are
# never changed or reused. Write for the player, in plain words.

@ 20261122-fists-element 2026-11-22 Trentlin
You reported a journeyman assassin "unaffected" by the first two blows of
your fists of fury.  Thank you -- it was working as built, but nothing told
you why.  Each strike of the fury carries its own element (acid,
lightning, cold, fire, then edged, piercing and plain blows), and the
journeyman assassin is immune to fire and cold, so those two strikes did
nothing.

Each strike now names its element as it lands -- "blazing fists of fury",
"frost-wreathed fists of fury" and so on -- so an immune foe reads as
immune to that element, not to your fists.  HELP FISTS OF FURY explains it.

@ 20261122-iron-skin 2026-11-22 Trentlin
You reported being hit by slashing blows while iron skin should have made
you immune.  Thank you -- iron skin did make you immune to slashing, but it
lasts only a tick or two (a minute or so of play), and it wore off
mid-fight.  Your recast then drew no immunity at all, which it does one
time in four, and did not say so.

Iron skin now says when a cast turns no blow aside, and its wear-off line
says that blows hurt you as before.  HELP IRON SKIN has the details.

@ 20261122-quest-coin 2026-11-22 Trentlin
You asked whether 170 platinum for a quest on a 35-quest streak was too
much.  Thank you -- you were right that quests paid too much coin.  Your
streak raises only quest points, not coin, but quests were paying four to
twelve kills' worth of coin at your level (twice that on a rush), and they
had become most of your income.

Quest coin is now about half that: two to six kills' worth for a hunt,
three to six for a recovery, still doubled on a rush.  Quest points and
your streak bonus are unchanged.
